<style>
  @page {
    size: A4;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .page {
    width: 794px;
    height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden;
    page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child {
    page-break-after: auto;
  }
  h1, h2, h3 {
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  .header-section {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
  }
  .metadata-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .metadata-table td {
    padding: 5px 0;
  }
  .content-section {
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .highlight {
    font-weight: bold;
  }
</style>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-section">
    <h1 style="text-align: center;">JACKSONVILLE STATE UNIVERSITY</h1>
    <h2 style="text-align: center;">Office of Human Resources</h2>
  </div>

  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <h3 style="margin-bottom: 5px;">MEMORANDUM</h3>
  </div>

  <table class="metadata-table">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 100px;">TO:</td>
      <td><span data-field="recipient_group">{{ recipient_group }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>FROM:</td>
      <td><span data-field="sender_department">{{ sender_department }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>DATE:</td>
      <td><span data-field="date_issued">{{ date_issued }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>SUBJECT:</td>
      <td><span data-field="subject">{{ subject }}</span></td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2 style="font-weight: bold;">PEEHIP INSURANCE COVERAGE</h2>
    <p>The 2012-2013 Open Enrollment period started on <span data-field="start_date">{{ start_date }}</span> and will continue through <span data-field="end_date">{{ end_date }}</span> for changes to become effective <span data-field="effective_date">{{ effective_date }}</span>. Again this year PEEHIP will <span class="highlight">NOT BE</span> mailing the Open Enrollment Booklet to members, instead all active and retired members should be receiving a <span class="highlight">one page notice</span>, which will inform you of the current coverage you are enrolled and specifics of the open enrollment period. PEEHIP now has the Open Enrollment booklet available on their website, and you can also find the booklet on the HR “Open Enrollment” webpage. Members can download the information and forms, or members can make changes using the Member Online system (recommended).</p>

    <p>All Open Enrollment forms should be mailed directly to PEEHIP and must be postmarked no later than <span data-field="mailing_deadline">{{ mailing_deadline }}</span> for the PEEHIP office to accept the request. Members will have until <span data-field="final_deadline">{{ final_deadline }}</span> to make open enrollment changes through the Member Online Services system. To get more information on the online system please go to the RSA Website at <span data-field="website_url">{{ website_url }}</span> and click the “Member Online Services” link on the left side of the page. For those members who do not have internet access and cannot download the information, they can contact PEEHIP at <span data-field="contact_phone">{{ contact_phone }}</span> to have a packet mailed.</p>

    <p>Members who want to enroll or continue participation in the PEEHIP Flexible Spending Accounts and the Federal Poverty Level Premium Discount program, are required to <span class="highlight">re-enroll each year</span>. These two programs do not automatically renew each year without a new application, regardless to whether or not you are making changes.</p>

    <p>If you do not wish to make changes to your PEEHIP coverage, do not complete the open enrollment application (with the exceptions of the above plans). You will automatically remain enrolled in the same or existing plan(s). Your monthly premium will continue to be deducted from your paycheck.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Humana/CompBenefits Vision Plan</h3>
    <p>The Open Enrollment period for the CompBenefits Vision Plan starts <span data-field="vision_start_date">{{ vision_start_date }}</span> and ends <span data-field="vision_end_date">{{ vision_end_date }}</span> for changes to become effective <span data-field="vision_effective_date">{{ vision_effective_date }}</span>. The CompBenefits plan is not part of the PEEHIP benefits package; this is a stand alone plan and Open Enrollment forms can be picked up and should be returned to the Office of Human Resources (<span data-field="office_location">{{ office_location }}</span>) no later than <span data-field="vision_deadline">{{ vision_deadline }}</span>. If you are currently enrolled in PEEHIP’s Vision plan and are planning to change to CompBenefits or vice versa you must remember to cancel the other coverage; this does <span class="highlight">NOT happen automatically</span>. Failing to cancel the other coverage will result in your being enrolled and paying premiums for both vision plans for an entire plan year. If you do not need to make changes to your CompBenefits Vision Plan, then you NEED TO DO NOTHING.</p>

    <p>For more information on PEEHIP changes occurring effective <span data-field="info_date">{{ info_date }}</span>, please join us at one of the on-campus sessions <span data-field="session_date">{{ session_date }}</span>, or refer to PEEHIP’s website at <span data-field="website_url_2">{{ website_url_2 }}</span>. As always if you have questions regarding these and other JSU Benefits, please feel free to contact the Office of Human Resources at ext. <span data-field="extension_number">{{ extension_number }}</span>.</p>
  </div>
</div>